      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: TEMPERATURE (EXTREMELY DETAILED)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Temperature distribution is influenced by latitude, altitude, ocean currents, continentality, and cloud cover.",
        "Temperature inversion occurs when warm air lies above cool air near the surface, acting as an exam-favorite concept.",
        "Global air pressure belts are formed due to thermal and dynamic factors across different latitudes.",
        "Wind dynamics are primarily driven by pressure gradient force, Coriolis force, and surface friction.",
        "Seasonal shifting of pressure belts creates major climate systems like monsoon winds."
      ],
      "id": "t4rv3u9"
